reached\": false, \"source\": 826, \"target\": 1460, \"window\": [3683, 42083]}", "latency_ms": 5, "tokens_before": 31843, "tokens_after": 31843, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "temporal_reachability", "args": {"source": 1885, "target": 765, "window": [3683, 42083]}, "result_digest": "17c980f53395f801", "result_summary": "{\"max_wait\": null, \"n_nodes_reached\": 2, \"reached\": false, \"source\": 1885, \"target\": 765, \"window\": [3683, 42083]}", "latency_ms": 10, "tokens_before": 40956, "tokens_after": 40956, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "top_active_nodes", "args": {"k": 5, "window": [3683, 42083]}, "result_digest": "051160957c8e90d5", "result_summary": "{\"top\": [{\"events\": 317, \"node\": 733}, {\"events\": 196, \"node\": 1566}, {\"events\": 181, \"node\": 81}, {\"events\": 162, \"node\": 1132}, {\"events\": 158, \"node\": 302}], \"window\": [3683, 42083]}", "latency_ms": 4, "tokens_before": 40956, "tokens_after": 40956, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_049448d4", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1885, 1460, 1572, 826, 765, 1045], "window": [3683, 42083], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 1885 to 1460. Under delta<=600 node 1885 reaches only 2 nodes, and even with unbounded waiting the frontier stays at 2 nodes, so the failure is not an artifact of the gap threshold. 1885's only out-neighbour is 1572, whose only out-neighbour is 826; neither 1572 (unbounded) nor 826 (delta<=600) reaches 1460, so the forward chain dissipates within two hops. Meanwhile 1460 is only ever contacted by 765 and 1045, and 1885 cannot temporally reach 765 at all. Path enumeration returns zero routes. Ambient volume (7236 events), overlapping activity bins for the focal nodes, and the unrelated activity hubs are controlled and do not yield a valid route."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\nThe evidence is decisive and consistent: no cascade exists.\n\n**Forward frontier from 1885 is essentially dead.** With the 600-unit constraint, 1885 reaches only 2 nodes total (step_01) \u2014 and critically, even with *unbounded* waiting the frontier is still only 2 nodes (step_03). This rules out the \"the gap constraint was too strict\" explanation: the failure is structural/temporal, not a matter of the 600-unit threshold.\n\n**The chain physically terminates.** 1885 has just 4 events and a single out-neighbour, 1572 (step_04, step_06). 1572 in turn has 2 events and one out-neighbour, 826 (step_09, step_10). From 1572 the unbounded frontier is 5 nodes and still misses 1460 (step_13); from 826 the \u03b4\u2264600 frontier is 4 nodes and also misses 1460 (step_14). The out-directed chain dissipates within two hops.\n\n**1460's in-edges come from a disjoint region.** 1460 is only ever contacted by 765 and 1045 (step_07, step_12), and 1885 cannot temporally reach 765 even with unbounded wait (step_15). Enumerating routes returns zero paths (step_08).\n\n**Confounders controlled.** The window is busy \u2014 7,236 events over 1,950 nodes (step_02) \u2014 and the six focal nodes are active in overlapping bins, e.g. 7 events each in [27683, 32482] and [32483, 37282] (step_11). So co-activity and ambient volume alone could have suggested a cascade, but neither the popularity hubs (733, 1566, 81, 1132, 302 \u2014 step_16, none of which are on the 1885 chain) nor concurrent activity produces an actual time-respecting route. Both endpoints are low-degree peripheral nodes (4 and 3 events), not hubs.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_049448d4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460, 1572, 826, 765, 1045],\n  \"window\": [3683, 42083],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1885 to 1460. Under delta<=600 node 1885 reaches only 2 nodes, and even with unbounded waiting the frontier stays at 2 nodes, so the failure is not an artifact of the gap threshold. 1885's only out-neighbour is 1572, whose only out-neighbour is 826; neither 1572 (unbounded) nor 826 (delta<=600) reaches 1460, so the forward chain dissipates within two hops. Meanwhile 1460 is only ever contacted by 765 and 1045, and 1885 cannot temporally reach 765 at all. Path enumeration returns zero routes. Ambient volume (7236 events), overlapping activity bins for the focal nodes, and the unrelated activity hubs are controlled and do not yield a valid route.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 50462, "total_output_tokens": 4183, "total_tokens": 54645, "total_latency_ms": 58102, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}